@startuml
title Chain of Responsibility Pattern: Customer Support System

skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
left to right direction

' ============================================================
' 1. REQUEST TYPES
' ============================================================

enum Severity {
    Low
    Medium
    High
}

class Ticket <<Request>> {
    + severity : Severity
    + description : std::string
}

' ============================================================
' 2. ABSTRACT HANDLER
' ============================================================

abstract class SupportHandler <<Handler>> {
    - next_ : SupportHandler*
    # forward(ticket : const Ticket&) : void
    + setNext(next : SupportHandler*) : void
    + {abstract} handle(ticket : const Ticket&) : void
    + ~SupportHandler()
}

' ============================================================
' 3. CONCRETE HANDLERS
' ============================================================

class Level1Handler <<ConcreteHandler>> {
    + handle(ticket : const Ticket&) : void
}

class Level2Handler <<ConcreteHandler>> {
    + handle(ticket : const Ticket&) : void
}

class Level3Handler <<ConcreteHandler>> {
    + handle(ticket : const Ticket&) : void
}

' ============================================================
' 4. ENTRY-POINT ROUTER
' ============================================================

class TicketRouter <<Router>> {
    - level1_ : SupportHandler&
    - level2_ : SupportHandler&
    - level3_ : SupportHandler&
    + TicketRouter(level1 : SupportHandler&, level2 : SupportHandler&, level3 : SupportHandler&)
    + route(ticket : const Ticket&) : void
}

' ============================================================
' 5. INHERITANCE
' ============================================================

SupportHandler <|-- Level1Handler
SupportHandler <|-- Level2Handler
SupportHandler <|-- Level3Handler

' ============================================================
' 6. CHAIN AND REFERENCE RELATIONSHIPS
' ============================================================

' Non-owning successor pointer.
SupportHandler --> "0..1" SupportHandler : next_ (non-owning)

' Actual successor configuration in main().
Level1Handler ..> Level2Handler : setNext(&level2)
Level2Handler ..> Level3Handler : setNext(&level3)

' The router holds three non-owning handler references.
TicketRouter --> "3" SupportHandler : level1_, level2_, level3_\n(non-owning references)

' Request dependencies.
SupportHandler ..> Ticket : handle / forward
TicketRouter ..> Ticket : route
Ticket ..> Severity : severity

' ============================================================
' 7. HANDLER RESPONSIBILITIES
' ============================================================

note bottom of Level1Handler
  Handles Low.
  Forwards Medium and High.
end note

note bottom of Level2Handler
  Handles Low and Medium.
  Forwards High.
end note

note bottom of Level3Handler
  Handles all severity levels.
  Last handler in the chain.
end note

' ============================================================
' 8. ROUTING RULES AND OWNERSHIP
' ============================================================

note right of TicketRouter
  Initial entry-point priority:
  1. "urgent" -> Level 3
  2. "vip"    -> Level 2
  3. otherwise -> Level 1

  Substring matching is case-sensitive.
end note

note top of SupportHandler
  The client (main) owns handler objects.
  next_ does not manage their lifetimes.
end note

@enduml
